From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcrt, msvcp140: __GetPlatformExceptionInfo and Concurrency::details::_ReportUnobservedException.

__GetPlatformExceptionInfo (msvcr120, ucrtbase, forwarded by vcruntime140
and msvcr120_app) looks at the C++ exception being handled: it reports
whether it is a std::bad_alloc (or a type deriving from it) and returns no
WinRT information (C++/CX Platform::Exception records log a FIXME).
Concurrency::details::_ReportUnobservedException (msvcr110, msvcr120,
msvcp140, forwarded by msvcp_win and msvcr120_app) ends the program through
terminate(): an exception of a task that nobody observed is fatal, as the
Concurrency Runtime documents. Both were spec stubs called by Edge and
Audacity.
